{"text": "Looking at this problem, I need to find 34462116119303 mod 650.\n\n## Step 1: Find the quotient and remainder using division\n\nLet me work through this systematically by successive divisions:\n\n- 650 \u00d7 50,000,000,000 = 32,500,000,000,000\n- Remainder: 34,462,116,119,303 - 32,500,000,000,000 = 1,962,116,119,303\n\n- 650 \u00d7 3,000,000,000 = 1,950,000,000,000  \n- Remainder: 1,962,116,119,303 - 1,950,000,000,000 = 12,116,119,303\n\n- 650 \u00d7 18,000,000 = 11,700,000,000\n- Remainder: 12,116,119,303 - 11,700,000,000 = 416,119,303\n\n- 650 \u00d7 600,000 = 390,000,000\n- Remainder: 416,119,303 - 390,000,000 = 26,119,303\n\n- 650 \u00d7 40,000 = 26,000,000\n- Remainder: 26,119,303 - 26,000,000 = 119,303\n\n- 650 \u00d7 180 = 117,000\n- Remainder: 119,303 - 117,000 = 2,303\n\n- 650 \u00d7 3 = 1,950\n- Remainder: 2,303 - 1,950 = **353**\n\n## Step 2: Verify\n\nThe quotient sum: 50,000,000,000 + 3,000,000,000 + 18,000,000 + 600,000 + 40,000 + 180 + 3 = 53,018,640,183\n\nCheck: 650 \u00d7 53,018,640,183 + 353 = 34,462,116,119,303 \u2713\n\n## Final Answer\n\n**353**", "usage": {"calls": 1, "input_tokens": 1237, "output_tokens": 5710, "cost_usd": 0.029786999999999998, "latency_s": 35.3577561378479}, "model": "claude-haiku-4-5-20251001", "stop_reason": "end_turn"}